{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"reasoning","text":"We have code. Root cause: createConfigCache caches the rejected promise in Map. After failure, entries.set(key, pending) holds a rejected promise. Next getConfig sees pending truthy and awaits rejected, rethrowing. Need remove entry on rejection so next read calls origin. Also must handle concurrent misses share one in-flight load; failure cleanup remove only matching failed load: if entry was cleared and replaced while first load running, late failure must not remove replacement. This suggests removal must use reference identity: only delete from map if current value === pending (the promise that failed). Also not poison future reads. Need ensure successful entries not evicted. So fix: wrap pending promise, on catch remove from entries if still same pending reference. For first failure, remove. For replacement case, current entry is different promise; don't delete. Need also handle invalid origin result? A failed or invalid origin result must not poison future reads. TypeError from normalizeConfig is thrown inside then chain, promise rejected; catch removes entry if current same. Good. Need ensure concurrent misses for same tenant share one load; yes entries.set before promise resolves. Need independent copies; copyConfig.\n\nAPI contract: JSON responses, no-store etc. Already. Invalid tenant: TypeError with tenantId message => 400. Good.\n\nNeed add three meaningful tests in student-tests. Must not skip/todo/placeholder. Could test: \n1) cache retries after promise rejection and removes failed load (incident).\n2) late failure of replaced load does not delete replacement entry.\n3) successful entries not evicted after unrelated failure? Or invalid config result does not poison subsequent reads. Or failure cleanup removes only matching failed load. Also test that a successful load is not removed by a stale failure from previous load. Need design.\n\nNeed run node --test ... Let's first reproduce failure? Existing committed test already includes \"retries the origin after a transient load failure\" which should currently fail. Let's run."}}
