c Test.processPendingSubtests (node:internal/test_runner/test:831:7)\n\ntest at benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.test.mjs:59:1\n✖ the API recovers on the request after a transient origin failure (1.638958ms)\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Expected values to be strictly equal:\n  \n  503 !== 200\n  \n      at TestContext.<anonymous> (file:///private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-2Y8l4T/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.test.mjs:75:10)\n      at async Test.run (node:internal/test_runner/test:1208:7)\n      at async Test.processPendingSubtests (node:internal/test_runner/test:831:7) {\n    generatedMessage: true,\n    code: 'ERR_ASSERTION',\n    actual: 503,\n    expected: 200,\n    operator: 'strictEqual',\n    diff: 'simple'\n  }\n\ntest at benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs:4:1\n✖ replace this placeholder with incident regression tests (1.615667ms)\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Add at least three meaningful tests\n      at TestContext.<anonymous> (file:///private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-2Y8l4T/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs:5:10)\n      at Test.runInAsyncScope (node:async_hooks:226:14)\n      at Test.run (node:internal/test_runner/test:1201:25)\n      at Test.start (node:internal/test_runner/test:1096:17)\n      at startSubtestAfterBootstrap (node:internal/test_runner/harness:385:17) {\n    generatedMessage: false,\n    code: 'ERR_ASSERTION',\n    actual: undefined,\n    expected: undefined,\n    operator: 'fail',\n    diff: 'simple'\n  }\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"reasoning","text":"Tests confirm root cause. Now we need edit config-cache.mjs. We can only edit allowed files. Let's consider precise implementation.\n\nCurrent:\n```\nlet pending = entries.get(key);\nif (!pending) {\n  pending = Promise.resolve()\n    .then(() => loadFromOrigin(key))\n    .then(normalizeConfig);\n  entries.set(key, pending);\n}\nreturn copyConfig(await pending);\n```\nNeed to remove rejected promise from cache. We can attach `.catch` to pending that deletes from map only if entries.get(key) === pending. However if promise is awaited and rejected, catch handler runs after rejection and after await throws. But catch is attached before awaiting? We build pending then attach catch. Need ensure catch runs even if caller awaits and sees error. Promise rejection is consumed by catch. Good.\n\nBut caution: If we attach catch to pending, the catch returns undefined/resolves? Then if we await pending, it might not throw? Actually attaching a catch handler creates a new promise chain, not mutate pending. `await pending` sees the original promise state, which is rejected. The attached catch is a separate consumer and will run but doesn't change pending's state. So await pending throws. Good. In catch, entries.delete? Use reference identity: if entries.get(key) === pending then entries.delete(key). That handles replacement: if entry was cleared and replaced, current entry is different or none, so don't delete. Also handles explicit clear before failure: entries.get(key) maybe undefined, no deletion.\n\nBut need ensure successful entries not evicted by a stale failure from a prior load. Since on success entries.set(key, pending) remains; later if somehow same pending fails? It can't, resolved promise can't reject. Replacement scenario: first load pending in map, then clear(\"acme\") removes pending from map, entries.set new pending (call count 2). First load late rejects; catch checks entries.get(key) === oldPending? false, no delete. Good.\n\nWhat if clear() is called while first load in flight but no replacement set yet. entries.get(key) undefined. Late failure no delete. Good.\n\nWhat if entries.delete on catch after second load success: entries.get(key) === oldPending false. Good.\n\nNeed maybe handle normalizeConfig throwing TypeError or load throwing. Since catch catches any rejection of pending. Good.\n\nNeed maintain coalescing? On failure removal, next read creates new promise. Good.\n\nOne subtlety: The catch handler returns undefined, but unhandled rejection? No, catch consumes.\n\nAlternative: Use try/catch around await and delete then rethrow. But if concurrent callers await same pending, one catches? No, easier to attach catch. Let's implement:\n\n```\nlet pending = entries.get(key);\nif (!pending) {\n  pending = Promise.resolve()\n    .then(() => loadFromOrigin(key))\n    .then(normalizeConfig);\n  entries.set(key, pending);\n  pending.catch(() => {\n    if (entries.get(key) === pending) {\n      entries.delete(key);\n    }\n  });\n}\nreturn copyConfig(await pending);\n```\nNeed maybe if pending already exists but is rejected? Actually after catch removal, entries won't have rejected promise. If entry exists, it's either resolved or in-flight. Good.\n\nLet's patch config-cache.mjs. Also need maybe import? No.\n\nNow tests for student-tests.mjs. Must cover incident and behavior broken by overly broad fix. Cases:\n1. \"retries origin after a rejected load instead of poisoning the cache\" — already exists in config-cache.test.mjs, but can include a focused student test. Need at least three meaningful. Avoid duplicate? It's fine but maybe cover other angles.\n2. \"a stale failure from a cleared/replaced load does not evict the replacement\" — exactly matching requirement.\n3. \"invalid origin results do not poison future reads\" — normalizeConfig throws TypeError, entry removed, retry returns config. This guards overly broad fix that might only catch ConfigOriginError.\n4. \"successful entries survive a later unrelated cache miss\" — maybe not needed.\n5. \"failure cleanup uses identity so successful entries are not deleted\" — similar to replacement.\n\nLet's design tests with clear mechanics.\n\nTest 1: incident regression: a transient origin error is retried and API returns 200 on next request.\n```\ntest('retries after a rejected origin load and recovers through the API', async () => {\n  let calls=0; const cache = createConfigCache(async () => { calls++; if (calls===1) throw new ConfigOriginError('timeout'); return CONFIG; }); const handle=createConfigApi(cache);\n  const first = await handle({method:'GET',url:'/api/config/acme'}); assert.equal(first.status,503); assert.equal(first.headers['retry-after'],'1');\n  const second = await handle({method:'GET',url:'/api/config/acme'}); assert.equal(second.status,200); assert.deepEqual(second.body,{config:CONFIG}); assert.equal(calls,2);\n});\n```\nThis covers incident.\n\nTest 2: stale failure of replaced load does not remove replacement.\n```\ntest('late failure of a replaced load does not delete the replacement entry', async () => {\n  let calls=0; let releaseFirst; let releaseSecond;\n  const origin = (key) => new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n     calls++;\n     if (calls===1) releaseFirst = () => reject(new ConfigOriginError('first timeout'));\n     else releaseSecond = () => resolve(CONFIG);\n  });\n  const cache = createConfigCache(origin);\n  const p1 = cache.getConfig('acme'); // miss, call 1\n  // Now clear and replace while first in-flight\n  cache.clear('acme');\n  const p2 = cache.getConfig('acme'); // miss, call 2\n  releaseFirst(); // first fails late\n  assert.rejects(p1, ConfigOriginError);\n  // The replacement should still be in flight/ pending; resolve it\n  releaseSecond();\n  const second = await p2;\n  assert.deepEqual(second, CONFIG);\n  // Entry should remain cached; subsequent read hits\n  const third = await cache.getConfig('acme');\n  assert.deepEqual(third, CONFIG);\n  assert.equal(calls, 2);\n});\n```\nNeed ensure releaseSecond defined. Since second load triggered after clear, calls=2, so releaseSecond set. But if p2 already resolved by releaseSecond after first failure, fine. However p2 might resolve after releaseSecond. Need p2 awaited after releaseSecond. Good.\n\nBut subtle: p1 is the original promise that will reject. After cache.clear('acme'), entries map has p2. pending.catch on p1 will run when releaseFirst; entries.get(key) === p1? false; no delete. Then resolve p2. Good.\n\nTest 3: invalid origin result does not poison future reads.\n```\ntest('invalid origin responses are not cached and are retried', async () => {\n  let calls=0;\n  const cache = createConfigCache(async () => {\n    calls++;\n    if (calls===1) return { version: 123, features: [] }; // invalid version type\n    return CONFIG;\n  });\n  await assert.rejects(cache.getConfig('acme'), TypeError);\n  const config = await cache.getConfig('acme');\n  assert.deepEqual(config, CONFIG);\n  assert.equal(calls,2);\n});\n```\nThis ensures any rejection removed, not just ConfigOriginError.\n\nOr test that failure cleanup only deletes matching entry (replacement) already. Good.\n\nNeed maybe include API contract? Already config-cache.test covers. But important behavior broken by overly broad fix: if fix clears entire map on any failure, different tenants entries cleared. Could test that failure for one tenant doesn't clear other tenant entry. But requirement says failure cleanup remove only matching failed load. A broad fix might call entries.clear() on any rejection; this would evict successful entries. We can test to guard:\n```\ntest('a failure for one tenant does not evict cached configs for another tenant', async () => {\n  const results = { acme: 'ok', beta: 'error' };\n  let calls = 0;\n  const cache = createConfigCache(async (tenantId) => {\n    calls++;\n    if (tenantId === 'beta') throw new ConfigOriginError('beta down');\n    return CONFIG;\n  });\n  await cache.getConfig('acme');\n  await assert.rejects(cache.getConfig('beta'), ConfigOriginError);\n  // acme should still be cached (no extra origin call)\n  const acmeAgain = await cache.getConfig('acme');\n  assert.deepEqual(acmeAgain, CONFIG);\n  assert.equal(calls, 2);\n});\n```\nThis is good. But already test 2 covers identity. We can include both.\n\nNeed at least three. Let's include:\n- incident regression via API (or cache)\n- stale replacement identity\n- invalid origin response retry\n- maybe failure doesn't clear other tenants (4th) – allowed. User said at least three. More is okay? Keep meaningful.\n\nBut must be careful: in replacement test, releaseSecond assignment. Need ensure it's defined when second origin call happens. In our origin function, when calls===2, set releaseSecond. But second load is triggered after clear before releaseFirst. So origin call happens, calls becomes 2, releaseSecond set. Good. Then after releaseSecond, p2 resolves. But what about p2 after releaseSecond? We need to releaseSecond after asserting p1 rejects? p1 rejects when releaseFirst called. But we need not await p1 rejects before releaseSecond? It doesn't matter; releaseSecond resolves second promise. Then we await p1 rejects. Fine. However in `assert.rejects(p1, ConfigOriginError)`, after releaseFirst, p1 rejects. That assertion can be done after releaseSecond? p2 already resolved. Then `await p2` returns. Good. But one caveat: If we call `releaseFirst()` and then `releaseSecond()` immediately, p2 resolves. Then `assert.rejects(p1, ConfigOriginError)` may need to be awaited before subsequent; it returns a promise. Actually `assert.rejects(promise, error)` returns a promise that resolves if promise rejects. We can `await assert.rejects(p1, ConfigOriginError)`. Good.\n\nBut there is risk: p1 is the old pending from first load, after clear, its catch handler attempts delete only if entries.get(key) === p1. Since entries has p2, no delete. But p1 catch also does not throw. Good.\n\nHowever we need to ensure that after releaseFirst, p1 rejection is observed by its catch handler before p1 is garbage-collected? Since p1 is referenced by p1 variable and catch handler, fine.\n\nLet's write tests.\n\nNow need also update INCIDENT.md. Must describe user impact, root cause and code/log evidence, why healthy probe and repeated cache=hit lines misleading, fix, regression coverage, remaining risk. Plain language. Need include evidence from code/log. Keep within constraints. We'll write concise markdown.\n\nNeed edit only allowed files. config-api.mjs maybe no changes needed? We can leave as is. But if there's any bug in API contract? Let's verify: TypeError from invalid tenant: the cache throws TypeError with tenantId message. API catches TypeError & tenantId regex => 400. Good. But API uses `if (error instanceof TypeError && /tenantId/.test(error.message))` which catches both tenant validation and origin config errors that are TypeError. However normalizeConfig throws TypeError with message \"origin returned an invalid config\" etc, not tenantId, so not 400. Good. ConfigOriginError => 503 with retry-after. Other errors =>500.\n\nBut incident.log shows `cache=hit status=503 error=origin_timeout` after first. That suggests API logs cache hit on subsequent requests. Since cache holds rejected promise, yes. Healthy probe means origin is now healthy but cache still poisoned. The \"wrong direction\" is because one might think cache is serving stale error and probe healthy means cache problem; actually the cache is storing the rejected promise as if it were a valid hit.\n\nRoot cause: `entries.set(key, pending)` stores the promise before it resolves/rejects, and there is no cleanup on rejection. So once load fails, the rejected promise remains as cached \"hit\" indefinitely.\n\nFix: add `.catch` to pending to remove entry if it is still the current entry. Use identity to avoid deleting replacements.\n\nNow code patch. Use apply_patch. Need note tool? The instructions mention apply_patch tool. But available tools include exec_command and write_stdin. There is no apply_patch tool in tool list. We can use exec_command with cat > file or sed. The system says \"Use the apply_patch tool to edit files (NEVER try applypatch or apply-patch, only apply_patch): ...\" but tool is not present. In these environments, we can use `cat > file <<'EOF'` or similar via exec_command. Use exec_command to overwrite file with modified content. Need preserve exact content. Let's compose. Could use `cat > benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.mjs <<'EOF'` and paste content.\n\nSimilarly for student-tests and INCIDENT.\n\nLet's make plan update."}}
