{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"**Root cause**\n\n`config-cache.mjs` stored the in-flight promise in the `Map` before it resolved. When the origin load rejected, the rejected promise stayed in the cache, so every later `getConfig(\"acme\")` awaited the same rejection instead of trying the origin again. The log proves it: `cache=hit` keeps returning `origin_timeout` even after the origin probe shows `status=200`, and `origin_load_count=1` confirms only one load ever happened.\n\n**Changed files**\n\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.mjs` — added a `.catch` handler that removes the failed promise only when it is still the current entry, so a stale failure cannot wipe out a replacement.\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs` — replaced the placeholder with four regression tests: API recovery after a transient failure, replacement-entry survival, invalid-origin retry, and tenant-isolation of failures.\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/INCIDENT.md` — documented impact, root cause, misleading log signals, fix, regression coverage, and a remaining risk.\n\n**Verification**\n\n```bash\nnode --test benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs\n```\n\nResult: **9/9 pass**. `npx eslint` on the edited files also passes.\n\n**Remaining concern**\n\nThe cache has no TTL or expiration. Once a successful config is cached, it stays in memory until `clear()` is called or the process restarts, so config refresh must remain an explicit invalidation concern."}}
